## Premises (measured by the feed5 drafter at 05:47 on 2026-09-22 AEST, in a `--shared` scratchpad clone detached at 64ab10513; Wednesday re-derives before queueing)
- Ticket KS-811 (P4, Backlog, kamil.kreiser@secuura.ai, no PR attachment): "Add a test that derives both sets and compares them: the codes the spec publishes for the social-callback 403s, against the codes the route can throw." The product is RIGHT at the tip: the callback body (`routes/auth.ts:965-1291`) throws BadRequestError (400), OAuthProviderError (400), OAuthStateInvalidError (403 OAUTH_STATE_INVALID), SocialEmailUnavailableError (403 SOCIAL_EMAIL_UNAVAILABLE), SocialSignInRefusedError (403 SOCIAL_SIGN_IN_REFUSED) and MfaRequiredError (403 MFA_REQUIRED); the operation's 403 block (`auth.openapi.ts:2079-2102`, "Four distinct codes") names exactly OAUTH_STATE_INVALID, SOCIAL_SIGN_IN_REFUSED, SOCIAL_EMAIL_UNAVAILABLE, MFA_REQUIRED. The QA script's own run at #815's merge found three codes on each side; the tip has four (KS-722 added OAUTH_STATE_INVALID to both) - still equal. This is an AUTH TEST-ONLY pin (allowed); no auth product file is edited.
- The test file is ABSENT at 64ab10513 - ONE NEW FILE (`ls src/__tests__ | grep -c -i ks811` = 0). Mode NEW. Pure source-text cells: no app boot, no network, no Redis, no database (the ks622-retired-route-contract idiom, `readFileSync` + `join(__dirname, ...)`).
